e><surname>Nyamathi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Leake</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Keenan</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gelberg</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Type of social support among homeless women: Its impact on psychosocial resources, health and health behaviors, and use of health services</article-title><source>Nurs Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>318</fpage><lpage>326</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11093696</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00006199-200011000-00004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nwakeze</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Magura</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenblum</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Joseph</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Homelessness, Substance Misuse, and Access to Public Entitlements in a Soup Kitchen Population</article-title><source>Substance Use &#x00026; Misuse</source><year>2003</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>645</fpage><lpage>668</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12747400</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1081/JA-120017388</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dohan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Henderson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>From enabling to bootstrapping:  welfare workers' views of substance abuse and welfare reform</article-title><source>Contemp Drug Problems</source><year>2005</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>429</fpage><lpage>455</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="j